    <briefdescription>
<para>This class represents a function that is read from a sample profile. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>It comes with two forms: a string or a hash code. The latter form is the 64-bit <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_m_d5" kindref="compound">MD5</ref> of the function name for efficient storage supported by ExtBinary profile format, and when reading the profile, this class can represent it without converting it to a string first. When representing a hash code, we utilize the LengthOrHashCode field to store it, and Name is set to null. When representing a string, it is same as <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_string_ref" kindref="compound">StringRef</ref>. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
